-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  lex_splices_blanks.pcpp - Lexical: blanks after a backslash where no splice is read

  lex_splices_err_space's warning has two places it does not go: inside
  a block comment's body (a splice there changes nothing) and inside a
  raw string (never spliced: the backslash, the blank and the newline
  stay its text). So this module has a backslash and a blank before a
  newline in both and builds with no report.
  Its bytes are part of the test (see above): edit it with an editor
  that keeps them as they are.
*******************************************************************************/

module exe lex_splices_blanks;

/*
  @@test
    kind run
    expect
    | a\
    | b
    | [Heap] Allocs: 0, Frees: 0, Leaked: 0
  @@end
*/

begin
  /* a block comment \  
     goes on */
  println("{}", R"(a\ 
b)");
end.
